  "question": {
    "text": "A hanging block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;prevents the smaller block of mass <math> <mtext>m</mtext> </math> from slipping over a movable triangular block of mass <math> <mtext>M</mtext> </math>. All the surfaces are frictionless and the strings and the pulleys are light. Value of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;in terms of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math>&nbsp;is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0023_4eb98248c542.jpg\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 156px;\" />"
  },
